From 0d31d29c8ceccc9bb17e4920ff543dbd112c62a5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: macbox <macbox@localhost>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 16:13:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] read the release's pixel format table
 without a device

Reims answers whether Metal describes a pixel format, the format's name
and its block words from places that hold no device: a texture
descriptor's setPixelFormat:, its heap-layout rules and its CPU-write
unit. Up to a759d0e8 it read them from MetalLevel::pixel_format_info and
MetalLevel::describes, which took no device. ec72c052 removed MetalLevel
and left the table reachable only through Device::pixel_format_info and
Device::texture_level_info, whose answers no device decides (both just
call the crate-private table functions). The alternatives on Reims's
side were to make or look up a Vulkan device for every such answer, or
to copy the table.

PixelFormatInfo::of(raw) and TextureLevelInfo::of(&query) answer the
same table without a device: the same functions the Device methods
call, so nothing a device answers changes. api_signatures.tsv
re-blessed with scripts/api-signatures/signatures.py --bless (two rows
added, nothing else moved).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
